Companion host tool for patch 0046 (mode_fabric_surgery).  Same
edits.bin wire format as host/gen_edits.py (same header + record
struct, same CRC-32 over [version|n_records|records]); imports
pack_edits/parse_edits/_parse_mask from gen_edits.py to keep the
format in one place.

Narrows the mask domain to {0x0000, 0xFFFF} with a clear error message
when an asymmetric mask is supplied, pointing the user at the
toolchain blocker.  First line of defense before SD-side packing —
the on-chip mode_fabric_surgery handler re-checks symmetry, so a
manually-packed SD with an asymmetric record would still be rejected,
but it's better to fail at host time than after a flash + reboot
cycle.

Smoke-tested:
  - --edit 10,4,0,0xFFFF  -> writes 24 B edits.bin, parses back to
    (x=10, y=4, n=0, mask=0xFFFF).
  - --edit 10,4,0,0x6996  -> SystemExit with the asymmetric-mask
    refusal pointing at the Quartus Lite blocker.

For mode g/G exploration (TPU LUT memory loader, no fabric edit),
use host/gen_edits.py — that file remains unrestricted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
